      "writtenOn": "2023-07-20T15:29:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So, thinking about this for a bit and the desired invariants on `SkGlyph`...\n\nI think we want `generateMetrics` to return an \"optional\" struct with the advance, bounds, mask format, and extra bits. Then the caller of `generateMetrics` (currently `SkScalerContext` can set these on the glyph and the strike can be the one friend of `SkGlyph`. An alternative is to have some protected setters on `generateMetrics` (so only subclasses of `SkScalerContext` can call them which then calls the setters on `SkGlyph`. However, I think I like the former rather than the latter.",
      "revId": "dae51f0fbc249c1a43399787172bc4c0b4094f07",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    }
